  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ford Motor has $668M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, recorded across 15,830 awards with an average award size of $42.2K. Obligations are up 40.9% year over year. Annual obligations have moved between $307M and $688M in the last six fiscal years: FY21 was $503M, FY22 was $688M, FY23 was $307M, FY24 was $580M, FY25 was $474M, and FY26 is $668M so far. The General Services Administration is the primary buyer for FY2026 to date with $668M in obligations. Automobile Manufacturing is the primary NAICS market for FY2026 to date with $668M in obligations. These figures are contract obligations unless noted otherwise for award-value tables, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The data show a concentrated federal relationship through one large buying agency and one dominant industry market, with a substantial year-over-year increase in obligations for the current fiscal year to date.",
